## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect per-tenant, private data path while supporting burst workloads, with per-tenant model versions, canary rollouts, and drift monitoring in AWS ML services.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint
- PrivateLink data residency
- Per-tenant Model Registry tags
- Canary rollouts and tenant routing
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo AWS SDK calls to register and route per-tenant models
const sm = new SageMaker({region: 'us-east-1'});
sm.registerModel({ModelName:'tenantA-v2', ...});
sm.createEndpoint({EndpointName:'multi-tenant-endpoint', ...});

// Lambda routing logic
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const tenant = event.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const modelName = `${tenant}-latest`;
  return await sm.invokeEndpoint({
    EndpointName: 'multi-tenant-endpoint',
    TargetModel: modelName,
    Body: JSON.stringify(event.body)
  });
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates knowledge of edge ML deployment, covering model optimization, over-the-air updates, and monitoring strategies for resource-constrained environments.

## Key Concepts
- Edge inference using SageMaker Edge Manager
- Model quantization (INT8) for ARM64 architecture
- OTA updates via AWS IoT Jobs with rollback slots
- Local telemetry and validation with intermittent connectivity

## Code Example
```javascript
// Model inference with latency tracking
const model = loadModel('arm_int8.tflite');
const t0 = performance.now();
const output = model.run(input);
const latency = performance.now() - t0;

// Emit telemetry for edge agent
emitTelemetry({ latency, outputQuality: evaluateQuality(output) });
```
